[0.45, "o", "Title:      \u001b[1mSeal Hosted AWS PVM Runtime Contract\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:     \u001b[1m\u001b[92mverified\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\r\nArchetype:  \u001b[95m\u001b[1mStrategic\u001b[0m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-01\u001b[0m - Deliver a new epic that turns Port's prepared-node x86_64 Firecracker/PVM demo into a real provider-backed `cloud-aws` hosted lane. (\u001b[2mVFgcPDfEj\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-02\u001b[0m - On a prepared x86_64 AWS Linux node, canonical `port control-plane prepare-pvm-node`, `port machine launch --machine cloud-aws`, `port machine status --machine cloud-aws`, and `port machine stop --machine cloud-aws` succeed through the live hosted control-plane and node-agent path. (\u001b[2mrun the live AWS hosted PVM workflow end to end\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-03\u001b[0m - Port owns an explicit AWS host-kit preparation and readiness contract that proves custom kernel, `pti=off`, patched `firecracker-pvm`, and PVM artifact-kit availability without a manual config-overlay dance. (\u001b[2mprepare a node and inspect doctor / status / imported inventory output\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-04\u001b[0m - Failure surfaces remain provider-aware and honest: missing host kit, wrong kernel, missing patched VMM, stale imported readiness, or missing PVM artifacts fail with actionable `cloud-aws` guidance and no fallback to the standard lane. (\u001b[2minspect canonical failure paths plus automated tests\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-05\u001b[0m - Scope stays x86_64 AWS hosted PVM only; arm64 remains research-only and GCP/Azure or broader scheduler rollout do not land in this mission. (\u001b[2mreview planning and implementation artifacts for explicit AWS-only boundaries\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mChildren\u001b[0m\r\n  Epics (1):\r\n    \u001b[1m\u001b[36mVFgcPDfEj\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - AWS Hosted PVM Preparation And Launch (\u001b[2mdone\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mLatest Log Entry\u001b[0m\r\n    2026-04-02T18:21:26\r\n"]
[1.8, "o", "$ sed -n '1,120p' .keel/missions/VFgcM1Zpu/CHARTER.md\r\n"]
[2.25, "o", "# Seal Hosted AWS PVM Runtime Contract - Charter\r\n\r\nArchetype: Strategic\r\n\r\n## Goals\r\n\r\n| ID | Description | Verification |\r\n|----|-------------|--------------|\r\n| MG-01 | Deliver a new epic that turns Port's prepared-node x86_64 Firecracker/PVM demo into a real provider-backed `cloud-aws` hosted lane. | board: VFgcPDfEj |\r\n| MG-02 | On a prepared x86_64 AWS Linux node, canonical `port control-plane prepare-pvm-node`, `port machine launch --machine cloud-aws`, `port machine status --machine cloud-aws`, and `port machine stop --machine cloud-aws` succeed through the live hosted control-plane and node-agent path. | manual: run the live AWS hosted PVM workflow end to end |\r\n| MG-03 | Port owns an explicit AWS host-kit preparation and readiness contract that proves custom kernel, `pti=off`, patched `firecracker-pvm`, and PVM artifact-kit availability without a manual config-overlay dance. | manual: prepare a node and inspect doctor / status / imported inventory output |\r\n| MG-04 | Failure surfaces remain provider-aware and honest: missing host kit, wrong kernel, missing patched VMM, stale imported readiness, or missing PVM artifacts fail with actionable `cloud-aws` guidance and no fallback to the standard lane. | manual: inspect canonical failure paths plus automated tests |\r\n| MG-05 | Scope stays x86_64 AWS hosted PVM only; arm64 remains research-only and GCP/Azure or broader scheduler rollout do not land in this mission. | manual: review planning and implementation artifacts for explicit AWS-only boundaries |\r\n\r\n## Constraints\r\n\r\n- Keep the canonical Port command model; do not add a second AWS-only command family.\r\n- Port owns the runtime and host-preparation contract; EC2 provisioning, IAM, DNS, and downstream GitOps remain out of scope.\r\n- Do not solve this by switching the target to bare metal or by silently reusing the standard Firecracker/KVM lane.\r\n- Keep `cloud-aws` as the canonical operator proof surface, not `cloud-generic`.\r\n\r\n## Halting Rules\r\n\r\n- DO NOT halt while `cloud-aws` PVM still depends on generic-node substitution, manual imported-inventory edits, or hand-wired config overlays to demonstrate readiness.\r\n- HALT when the new epic is done and a live AWS x86_64 prepared node proves canonical `prepare-pvm-node` plus `machine launch/status/stop` for `cloud-aws`, with provider-aware failure messaging.\r\n- YIELD if the remaining blocker is a product decision about whether Port builds the AWS host kit itself or consumes an external host-kit artifact.\r\n"]
[3.6, "o", "$ keel epic show VFgcPDfEj\r\n"]
[4.05, "o", "Title:     \u001b[1mAWS Hosted PVM Preparation And Launch\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:    \u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m\r\nCreated:   \u001b[2m2026-04-02 18:17:35\u001b[0m\r\nStarted:   \u001b[2m2026-04-02 18:25:37\u001b[0m\r\nUpdated:   \u001b[2m2026-04-02 19:17:50\u001b[0m\r\nCompleted: \u001b[2m2026-04-02 19:17:50\u001b[0m (\u001b[2m52m\u001b[0m)\r\nPath:      \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VFgcPDfEj/README.md\u001b[0m\r\nPRD:       \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VFgcPDfEj/PRD.md\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mProblem\u001b[0m\r\n  Port has a generic prepared-node x86_64 Firecracker/PVM proof, but it still lacks a real provider-backed cloud-aws hosted runtime contract on regular AWS VMs. Downstream infrastructure currently falls onto the wrong standard Firecracker/KVM lane because Port does not yet own the AWS-specific host-kit preparation, readiness import, and live cloud-aws PVM proof surface.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m: Turn \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mcloud-aws\u001b[0m into a real hosted PVM lane on prepared x86_64 AWS Linux nodes. (Canonical \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mprepare-pvm-node\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mmachine launch\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mmachine status\u001b[0m, and \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mmachine stop\u001b[0m complete against the live hosted control-plane and node-agent path. -> One live AWS hosted PVM proof using the canonical commands)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m: Make AWS prepared-host readiness explicit and Port-owned. (Port can prepare a node and prove imported readiness for host kit, custom kernel, \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mpti=off\u001b[0m, patched \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mfirecracker-pvm\u001b[0m, and PVM artifacts without manual overlays. -> One AWS host-kit preparation contract plus readiness evidence)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m: Keep failure behavior honest and provider-aware. (Missing AWS-specific prerequisites fail with actionable \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mcloud-aws\u001b[0m guidance and do not fall back to the standard Firecracker/KVM lane. -> One verified failure surface for each prerequisite class in scope)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mScope Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m(no scope drift detected)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mRequirement Coverage\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-01\u001b[39m - Port must expose an AWS prepared-host contract for x86_64 Linux nodes that verifies custom kernel, \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mpti=off\u001b[0m, patched \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mfirecracker-pvm\u001b[0m, and required PVM artifacts through canonical preparation and readiness surfaces.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFgclbAzD\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-02\u001b[39m - \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport control-plane prepare-pvm-node\u001b[0m must prepare or import the AWS-specific host-kit readiness required for \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mcloud-aws\u001b[0m on a prepared x86_64 AWS Linux node without manual config overlays.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFgclbAzD\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-02\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-03\u001b[39m - \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport machine launch --machine cloud-aws\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport machine status --machine cloud-aws\u001b[0m, and \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport machine stop --machine cloud-aws\u001b[0m must route through the prepared AWS hosted PVM lane and succeed against the live hosted control-plane/node-agent path.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFgclbQzC\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-04\u001b[39m - Port must reject missing or stale AWS PVM prerequisites with actionable \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mcloud-aws\u001b[0m guidance and must not substitute the standard Firecracker/KVM lane.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (2): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFgclbAzD\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-03\u001b[39m, \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFgclbQzC\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-02\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-05\u001b[39m - Port must publish a canonical hosted AWS PVM proof surface that demonstrates the live AWS workflow and documents the AWS-only scope boundary.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFgclbQzC\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-03\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-01\u001b[39m - The epic must preserve clear operator visibility through doctor, status, or imported-inventory surfaces so AWS readiness can be diagnosed without reading source code.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFgclbAzD\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-02\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-02\u001b[39m - Verification must include both live hosted AWS proof and focused automated coverage for routing and failure-path regressions.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFgclbQzC\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-03\u001b[39m - Planning and implementation artifacts must keep scope explicitly limited to x86_64 AWS hosted PVM.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (2): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFgclbAzD\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-01\u001b[39m, \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFgclbQzC\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-02\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mPress Release\u001b[0m\r\n  Status:     \u001b[2mnot authored\u001b[0m\r\n  Guidance:   optional; use for large user-facing value shifts\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mProgress\u001b[0m\r\n  Voyages:              2/2 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m2/2\u001b[39m\r\n  Stories:              4/4 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m4/4\u001b[39m\r\n  ETA:                  complete\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Strategy\u001b[0m\r\n  Techniques:\r\n    - AWS host preparation: Manual node preparation plus doctor/status/imported-readiness inspection\r\n    - Area: Method\r\n    - Failure behavior: Focused automated tests plus manual spot checks for missing prerequisites\r\n    - Hosted runtime path: Live \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mcloud-aws\u001b[0m launch/status/stop workflow through the hosted control-plane and node agent\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Readiness\u001b[0m\r\n  Criteria:              automated 4 | manual 12\r\n  Requirement coverage:  automated 2 | manual 4\r\n  Artifact inventory:    text 10 | media 1 | other 1\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVoyages\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFgclbAzD\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - AWS PVM Host Kit Preparation (\u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m)\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFgclbQzC\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - Cloud Aws PVM Runtime Proof (\u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m)\r\n"]
